//Friend Function

A friend function is a function that is not a member of the class, but it is allowed to access the class's private and protected members.

We declare it using the friend keyword.

class Student {
private:
    int age = 20;

public:
    friend void show(Student s);
};

void show(Student s) {
    cout << s.age;
}

Here:

show() is not a member function of Student.
But because it is declared as friend, it can access Student's private age.
Student s;
show(s);
Important

A friend function:

❌ Is not called using object.function()
✅ Is called like a normal function
✅ Can access private and protected members

Simple definition:

Friend function = a non-member function that is given permission to access a class's private and protected members.